<p class="sst-lead">The leftover freedom from the last scene &mdash; the <strong>cyclic reparametrization</strong> (where
the landmark indexing starts) &mdash; is resolved by <strong>cyclic Procrustes</strong> registration.</p>

<p>\[ \min_{p\in\mathcal{N},\,R\in O(d)} \big\| C(p)X - YR \big\|_F
\iff p_* = \operatorname*{argmax}_{p} \big\| Y^{\top} C(p) X \big\|_{*},\quad R_* = U V^{\top}. \]</p>

<div class="sst-frag">
  <p>Here the apple is registered against a phase-shifted, rotated copy of itself. The naive
  index-to-index pairing is tangled; cyclic Procrustes finds the cyclic offset \(p_*\) (the peak of
  \(\|Y^{\top}C(p)X\|_*\)) and the rotation \(R_*\), and the shapes snap together.</p>
  <p class="sst-note">Drag a landmark to add real undulation: registration still removes the phase and rotation,
  and the <em>residual</em> that remains is the genuine shape difference &mdash; exactly the separation SST is after.</p>
</div>
